://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/W.T._Pike_Contemporary_Biographies_London_%28illustrations%29_%28114a%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:W.T._Pike_Contemporary_Biographies_London_(illustrations)_(114a).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=135028724","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2023-07-26 17:04:02","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"W.T. Pike Contemporary Biographies London (illustrations) (114a)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD-old-70-expired|Nyay Mandir|Template Unknown (author)|CC-PD-Mark|PD-old missing SDC copyright status|W.T. Pike Contemporary Biographies (London), illustrations","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p><i>Contemporary Biographies</i>, by W.T. Pike, including \"London at the opening of the Twentieth Century\". (Pike's New Century Series no.15). Published in 1905 by W.T. Pike &amp; Co., 19 Grand Parade, Brighton. \n</p><p>The volumes in this series each contain an illustrated section about the county, followed by a list of short biographies (each with a photographic portrait) of men of the county who were alive at the time of publication (plus a few who had recently died). Each volume has an index to the illustrations of buildings and views of the county, and an index to the biographies. The London volume was available to subscribers as sections of the whole: this section covers bureaucrats: actuaries and insurance, accountants, and secretaries.a\n</p>\nShowing a photograph titled: <i>The Law Courts, Baroda, India. Architect, R.F. Chisholm, F.R.I.B.A.</i> This is Nyay Mandir, designed by Robert Fellowes Chisholm (1840–1915).","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1905","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<i>Contemporary Biographies</i>, by W.T. Pike, including \"London at the opening of the Twentieth Century\". (Pike's New Century Series no.15). Published in 1905 by W.T. Pike &amp; Co., 19 Grand Parade, Brighton.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Unknown author<span style=\"display: none;\">Unknown author</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<table class=\"licensetpl\" style=\"display:none\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span class=\"licensetpl_short\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_long\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_link_req\">false</span><span class=\"licensetpl_attr_req\">false</span>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; clear: both; margin: 0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-progressive-subtle, #f7f8ff); color: var(--color-base, #202122); border: var(--border-subtle, 2px solid #8888aa); border-spacing: 8px; padding: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"layouttemplate\" lang=\"en\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span title=\"Public domain\"><img alt=\"Public domain\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/PD-icon.svg/120px-PD-icon.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/PD-icon.svg/250px-PD-icon.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"196\" data-file-height=\"196\"></span></span>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>This work is in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:public domain\">public domain</a></b> in its country of origin and other countries and areas where the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries%27_copyright_le